      "public_event_index": "monitor/task_evidence/public_events.jsonl",
      "raw_arguments": "{\"message\": \"The NewAllStrings validator implementation is incorrect. \\n\\n**Requirement:** `NewAllStrings(validators ...fyne.StringValidator) fyne.StringValidator` - a validator combinator that runs all provided validators in sequence and returns the first error (or nil if all pass). This enables chaining multiple validators together.\\n\\n**Current implementation** in data/validation/strings.go: `NewAllStrings(valid []string)` - a whitelist validator that checks if input matches any string in a list.\\n\\nThis is a fundamental misunderstanding. NewAllStrings should:\\n1. Accept variadic `fyne.StringValidator` arguments (not a string slice)\\n2. Return a `StringValidator` that calls each provided validator in order\\n3. Return the first error encountered, or nil if all validators pass\\n\\nExample correct implementation:\\n```go\\nfunc NewAllStrings(validators ...fyne.StringValidator) fyne.StringValidator {\\n    return func(text string) error {\\n        for _, validator := range validators {\\n            if err := validator(text); err != nil {\\n                return err\\n            }\\n        }\\n        return nil\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nAlso, the requirement specifies the file should be `data/validation/all.go`, not `strings.go`.\\n\\nPlease correct this implementation before completion.\"}",
      "review_id": "c9d658748787451b982b817f398c0ce6",
      "timestamp": 1791053913.7922137
    }
  ],
